1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,729
the mind tries to edit reality.

2
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:12,173
We start with Alex, a smart but anxious mind, scrolling a text he just said out loud.

3
00:00:07,050 --> 00:00:08,588
(just make it perfect.)

4
00:00:14,350 --> 00:00:17,533
The clock ticks, the room feels still.

5
00:00:24,350 --> 00:00:27,739
The inner adviser surfaces, offering a helpful edit.

6
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:27,208
(what if they think you’re weird?)

7
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:33,339
It frames uncertainty as a flaw that must be fixed before sending.

8
00:00:40,250 --> 00:00:43,213
He starts polishing language, seeking clarity.

9
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:46,000
maybe too formal?

10
00:00:49,250 --> 00:00:53,133
Each rewrite feels like progress, yet the silence grows louder.

11
00:01:05,450 --> 00:01:06,950
...yeah.

12
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:10,086
Now the adviser asks for certainty.

13
00:01:08,250 --> 00:01:09,788
(you need a guarantee.)

14
00:01:15,550 --> 00:01:19,654
It turns a simple clarification into a demand for a response script.

15
00:01:22,150 --> 00:01:24,458
Did I say the right thing?

16
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:33,361
A pause in the night, a new light.

17
00:01:35,450 --> 00:01:38,400
The note reminds him that honesty beats perfection.

18
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:46,967
He decides to send the version that feels true, not safe.

19
00:01:43,850 --> 00:01:45,350
just send it.

20
00:01:53,450 --> 00:01:56,444
Sending creates a tiny rupture in the loop.

21
00:01:58,100 --> 00:02:03,338
The brain can no longer simulate the same outcome; it must wait for real feedback.

22
00:02:05,550 --> 00:02:09,192
The reply is a small misunderstanding, not a disaster.

23
00:02:06,100 --> 00:02:07,600
(just send it.)

24
00:02:14,600 --> 00:02:17,547
It invites a brief conversation, not a crisis.

25
00:02:14,850 --> 00:02:16,773
I thought you meant tomorrow.

26
00:02:16,850 --> 00:02:18,773
Oh! Let’s meet tomorrow then.

27
00:02:22,250 --> 00:02:27,369
The inner voice reverts to its original role: a factual adviser, not a perfectionist.

28
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:24,100
(keep it clear.)

29
00:02:29,300 --> 00:02:32,894
It helps craft the next message without demanding guarantees.

30
00:02:38,350 --> 00:02:42,598
Real interaction supplies the information the mind was trying to manufacture.

31
00:02:39,100 --> 00:02:41,023
Thanks for clearing that up!

32
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:42,100
Anytime.

33
00:02:44,200 --> 00:02:49,153
The overthinking loop dissolves when we accept that uncertainty is part of conversation.

34
00:02:59,850 --> 00:03:02,397
Overthinking thrives on endless loops.

35
00:03:07,850 --> 00:03:13,550
By acting with honest specificity, we let reality answer, and the mind can rest.

36
00:03:17,050 --> 00:03:22,944
Clarity is a verb, not a promise. Perfection is a noun that never arrives.
